<p>Jean-Luc Mélenchon, the 74-year-old leader of La France Insoumise, said Sunday that he will run in France’s 2027 presidential election, launching a fourth bid for the Élysée. He confirmed the decision in a TF1 interview, becoming one of the highest-profile candidates to formally enter the race. Mélenchon said he was running because of the “context and urgency” of domestic and international politics, citing the risk of war, climate change and an approaching economic and social crisis. The 2027 vote will choose a successor to Emmanuel Macron, who is barred from seeking a third consecutive term; former Prime Minister Édouard Philippe is also expected to run from the center-right, while Marine Le Pen faces a potential ban.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/8aumXchmupddJDP94sOhDGvP7Kx0kK1P3eA58hT0AlJ3yEMYuXJOcsfVG-HJTZCgcFefz8RjnrX-m7N265xgcOTj4EGxcx2DcRlfxI2r5-46uoKPbq5DU0KdbohU6kQz0Tq_qXL2VBrzECZPyq4-ZSzFaZa76metgcRH1IyvNLH60OhvxXVFx2ccChA1kLH4xxgeecmqSlTz9ltJr9I-O5M6dvNrYyUG5-Cp28P7viI5fONVSt0-9f6BoR9iZwQV' alt='La France Insoumise leader Jean-Luc Mélenchon poses ahead of an interview on TF1&#x27;s evening news programme, where he announced his 2027 presidential candidacy in Boulogne-Billancourt, outside Paris, on May 3, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Polling position: Politico reported that recent polls put Mélenchon at 10.5% to 13% in the first round, depending on which other candidates enter the race.</li><li>Earlier pledge: Several French reports noted that after the 2022 election, Mélenchon said that contest would be his last, or challenged allies to “do better,” before reversing course.</li><li>Stated rival: Stern reported that Mélenchon identified the National Rally as his main rival in the race.</li></ul><blockquote>Yes, I am a candidate - Jean-Luc Mélenchon</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Jean-Luc Mélenchon: Mélenchon framed the bid as an organised LFI campaign, saying the movement had “a team, a programme, one candidate” and was ready. (<a href='https://www.letemps.ch/articles/jean-luc-melenchon-confirme-l-evidence-il-sera-candidat-a-l-election-presidentielle-francaise-de-2027'>Le Temps</a>)</li><li>Laurence Sailliet, former LR MEP: Sailliet called Mélenchon’s candidacy “un signal d’alerte,” or a warning signal. (<a href='https://www.bfmtv.com/politique/la-france-insoumise/video-jean-luc-melenchon-candidat-pour-l-election-presidentielle-je-pense-que-c-est-un-signal-d-alerte-observe-laurence-sailliet-ancienne-deputee-europeenne-lr_VN-202605030342.html'>BFMTV</a>)</li><li>Pierre Jouvet, Socialist Party: Jouvet criticised the candidacy, saying that “plus personne ne veut de Jean-Luc Mélenchon, ni à gauche, ni dans le pays,” and describing him as the most disliked political figure in France. (<a href='https://www.franceinfo.fr/politique/melenchon/plus-personne-ne-veut-de-jean-luc-melenchon-ni-a-gauche-ni-dans-le-pays-estime-le-socialiste-pierre-jouvet_7982033.html#xtor=RSS-3-%5Bgeneral%5D'>Franceinfo</a>)</li><li>Clémence Guetté, LFI lawmaker: Guetté defended the move, saying it was time for someone on the left to present an alternative and a credible candidacy. (<a href='https://www.bfmtv.com/politique/la-france-insoumise/video-jean-luc-melenchon-candidat-pour-l-election-presidentielle-il-etait-temps-qu-a-gauche-quelqu-un-propose-une-alternative-et-une-candidature-credible-explique-clemence-guette-deputee-lfi_VN-202605030337.html'>BFMTV</a>)</li><li>Arthur Delaporte, Socialist Party lawmaker: Delaporte said Mélenchon was not the best option to beat the far right. (<a href='https://www.bfmtv.com/politique/la-france-insoumise/video-jean-luc-melenchon-candidat-pour-l-election-presidentielle-il-n-est-pas-la-meilleure-des-solutions-pour-battre-l-extreme-droite-declare-arthur-delaporte-depute-ps_VN-202605030347.html'>BFMTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3352293/french-hard-left-politician-melenchon-stand-2027-presidential-election'>Mel